.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_CLOSE 3 2026-08-12 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_close \- close an opened MPQ archive.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_close("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "mpq_archive"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Close the archive handle returned by an archive open or create function.
The function takes a handle, not an output pointer, and consumes it regardless
of whether releasing its resources succeeds.
.PP
The archive handle must not be used or closed again after this call, including
when finalization or output close reports an error. Independently owned clones
and logical member streams remain usable with a valid backing source; custom
callback contexts must remain valid through their last derived handle.
.PP
For a writable archive, close returns any previously latched writer error.
Otherwise an active member writer causes
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE
and is discarded without finishing it. With no active writer or latched
error, close finalizes the archive, including writing headers, tables and
any configured signatures. MPQE output also requires transport finalization.
.PP
For caller-owned output, an optional flush runs only after successful
finalization. The caller retains ownership of the callback context and
backing storage through close, including on failure. Persistence and
publication of the sink remain the caller's responsibility. The library
never closes or frees those resources or guarantees durability or atomic
publication. A failure can leave partial output.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
/* *owned is an open reader or writer that the caller owns. */
int32_t
close_archive(mpq_archive_s **owned)
{
    int32_t status = libmpq__archive_close(*owned);
    *owned = NULL; /* Consumed even if close failed. */
    return status;
}
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success or a negative libmpq error.
An earlier writer or finalization error takes precedence over a later
filesystem close failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST
The archive pointer is NULL.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE
An unfinished member remains active, or the output exceeds a format or
extent limit.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_READ
Read-back or a private MPQE staging read failed.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_WRITE
Writing output failed, or removing private temporary storage failed during
MPQE finalization or on the reader's last close. This also covers failure
to publish path-based MPQE output.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_CLOSE
Closing a library-owned file failed, or the sink's flush callback returned
a positive status.
.PP
Other finalization errors can propagate, including
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_SEEK
when positioning output fails and
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_MALLOC
when allocating finalization metadata fails. Negative sink callback
statuses propagate unchanged. Positive read and write
statuses map to
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_READ
and
.BR LIBMPQ_ERROR_WRITE ,
respectively.
